{"name":"Port Hope","hex":"#54c3c1","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Port Hope","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A municipality in Northumberland County, Ontario, Canada, on Lake Ontario.","A village in Huron County, Michigan, United States, on Lake Huron."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Port_Hope"}],"entries":[{"title":"Port Hope, Michigan","blocks":[{"text":"Port Hope is a village in Huron County of the U.S. state of Michigan. As of the 2020 census, Port Hope had a population of 293. The village is within Rubicon Township."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/PortHope-MI-01s.jpg/330px-PortHope-MI-01s.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Port_Hope%2C_Michigan","wikidata":"Q3316320"},{"title":"Port Hope, Ontario","blocks":[{"text":"Port Hope is a municipality in Eastern Ontario, Canada, about 109 km (68 mi) east of Toronto and 159 km (99 mi) west of Kingston. It is at the mouth of the Ganaraska River on the north shore of Lake Ontario, in the west end of Northumberland County. The private Trinity College School opened here in 1865."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Downtown_Port_Hope%2C_May_27_2026_%2801%29.jpg/330px-Downtown_Port_Hope%2C_May_27_2026_%2801%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Port_Hope%2C_Ontario","wikidata":"Q613870"},{"title":"Port","blocks":[{"text":"A port is a maritime facility comprising one or more wharves or loading areas, where ships load and discharge cargo and passengers. Although usually situated on a sea coast or estuary, ports can also be found far inland, such as Hamburg, Manchester and Duluth; these access the sea via rivers or canals. Because of their roles as ports of entry for immigrants as well as soldiers in wartime, many port cities have experienced dramatic multi-ethnic and multicultural changes throughout their histories."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Manhattan.jpg/330px-Manhattan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Port","wikidata":"Q44782"},{"title":"Hope","blocks":[{"text":"Hope is an optimistic state of mind that is based on an expectation of desirable outcomes with respect to events and circumstances in one's own life, or the world at large. As a verb, Merriam-Webster defines hope as \"to expect with confidence\" or \"to cherish a desire with anticipation\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Hopeful.jpg/330px-Hopeful.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hope","wikidata":"Q190507"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Port_Hope_Town_Hall%2C_May_27_2026_%2804%29.jpg/500px-Port_Hope_Town_Hall%2C_May_27_2026_%2804%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Port_Hope_Town_Hall%2C_May_27_2026_%2804%29.jpg/1280px-Port_Hope_Town_Hall%2C_May_27_2026_%2804%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Port_Hope_Town_Hall%2C_May_27_2026_%2804%29.jpg/500px-Port_Hope_Town_Hall%2C_May_27_2026_%2804%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APort_Hope_Town_Hall%2C_May_27_2026_(04).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Ganaraska_River_in_Port_Hope_N.jpg/500px-Ganaraska_River_in_Port_Hope_N.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Ganaraska_River_in_Port_Hope_N.j